# Trivy IaC findings accepted on purpose (CI job "iac"). Each is a constraint of the AWS Learner
# Lab or of the budget (DECISIONS D-38, §3 Known limitations); revisit them in a normal account.

# EKS secrets envelope encryption needs a customer-managed KMS key and a key policy for LabRole.
# Kubernetes Secrets here only mirror SSM SecureStrings (External Secrets).
AWS-0039

# Public EKS API endpoint, open to any address: there is no VPN or bastion, and kubectl and
# Terraform run from laptops and GitHub runners whose IPs change. Access still needs IAM
# (LabRole) through EKS access entries.
AWS-0040
AWS-0041

# Nodes get public IPs in public subnets: there is no NAT gateway (about USD 1/day, D-38).
# Security groups admit only the NLB and the cluster; RDS stays in private subnets.
AWS-0164
